<!-- MAIN INFORMATION SECTION -->
<section class="information-section">
    <div class="information-container">

        <!-- LEFT CONTENT -->
        <div class="information-content">

            <h2>ICMR-NAMS National Biostatistics Helpline</h2>

            <p>
                The ICMR-NAMS National Biostatistics Helpline is a collaborative
                venture between the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR)
                and the National Academy of Medical Sciences (NAMS). It is
                designed to assist postgraduate medical students and young
                researchers in medical colleges and research institutes with
                practical biostatistics challenges.
            </p>

            <p>
                The Helpline will be one of its kind, as experienced
                epidemiologists and biostatisticians of national and
                international repute will provide hand-holding support to
                students so that they can get answers to queries related to
                statistical methods in connection with their research /
                dissertation work.
            </p>

            <p>
                This service will be provided free of charge; students can
                book slots for virtual one-to-one interaction with experts.
                We encourage students pursuing MD/MS/DNB/DM/MCh/DrNB/PhD
                programmes or other researchers to use this platform and
                discuss issues related to sampling, sample size calculation
                etc. Our resource faculty will guide them in solving the
                problems.
            </p>

        </div>


        <!-- RIGHT ANNOUNCEMENT -->
